{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2205","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Simons and Making It Beautiful"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Those cling-on troubles that ride my stride — cough up the fee, or step aside."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"— SHUN, "},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/4hpmSSMqgesMBCc3GNopCF"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"TAKE IT AWAY"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a permutation$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ $$$r$$$ of length $$$m$$$, we call an index $$$i$$$ ($$$1\\le i\\le m$$$) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if $$$i=\\max(\\{r_1,r_2,\\ldots,r_i\\})$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Simons has a permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$, and he can perform the following operation on $$$p$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose two indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ ($$$1\\le i\\ne j\\le n$$$), then swap $$$p_i$$$ and $$$p_j$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find a permutation $$$q$$$ that can be obtained from $$$p$$$ by performing the above operation at most once, such that the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" indices in $$$q$$$ is minimized."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$A permutation of length $$$n$$$ is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ distinct integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in arbitrary order. For example, $$$[2,3,1,5,4]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is not a permutation ($$$2$$$ appears twice in the array), and $$$[1,3,4]$$$ is also not a permutation ($$$n=3$$$ but there is $$$4$$$ in the array). "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 500$$$) — the length of $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_1,p_2,\\ldots,p_n$$$ ($$$1\\le p_i\\le n$$$, all $$$p_i$$$-s are distinct) — the elements of $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print $$$n$$$ integers $$$q_1,q_2,\\ldots,q_n$$$ — the permutation you found."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple possible permutations, you may output any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n1 2\n4\n2 3 1 4\n5\n3 2 4 5 1\n1\n1\n8\n4 1 3 2 6 7 8 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 1\n2 4 1 3\n3 2 4 5 1\n1\n4 1 3 8 6 7 2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, Simons can obtain only two possible permutations: $$$[1,2]$$$ and $$$[2,1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For permutation $$$[1,2]$$$, we can see $$$1=\\max(\\{1\\})$$$ and $$$2=\\max(\\{1,2\\})$$$. So there are two "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" indices. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For permutation $$$[2,1]$$$, we can see $$$1\\ne\\max(\\{2\\})$$$ and $$$2=\\max(\\{2,1\\})$$$. So there is only one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" index. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, permutation $$$[2,1]$$$ has the minimum count of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" indices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, Simons can obtain permutation $$$[2,4,1,3]$$$ by choosing indices $$$2$$$ and $$$4$$$ to swap. There is only one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" index in the permutation:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\ne \\max(\\{2\\})$$$, so index $$$1$$$ is not "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2\\ne \\max(\\{2,4\\})$$$, so index $$$2$$$ is not "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3\\ne \\max(\\{2,4,1\\})$$$, so index $$$3$$$ is not "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$4=\\max(\\{2,4,1,3\\})$$$, so index $$$4$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ugly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, note that Simons does not perform the operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2205A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2205/problem/A"}